WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:01.592
(audience cheering)

00:00:01.592 --> 00:00:03.035
- All right, y'all,
we've got one last story

00:00:03.035 --> 00:00:04.740
we hope brings a smile to your face.

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:05.696
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:05.696 --> 00:00:08.670
(rock music)
(audience cheering)

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:10.920
It is no secret that I'm a huge advocate

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:13.080
of reading early and reading often,

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:14.610
but there just aren't many books

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:16.470
for kids who are visually impaired.

00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:19.050
That's why we want to shine
a light on a Detroit woman

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:21.360
who's printing children's books in braille

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:24.120
and getting them into the hands
of kids all over the world.

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:25.050
It's amazing.

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:27.660
It's the perfect story for
this Braille Literacy month.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:28.920
Let's say hi to Debra,

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:32.370
the founder of Seedlings
watching on WXYZ TV.

00:00:32.370 --> 00:00:33.954
What's up, Debra?
(audience cheering)

00:00:33.954 --> 00:00:35.846
- Hi, Kelly.

00:00:35.846 --> 00:00:38.610
I was breathing really
fast, I'm so excited.

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:40.410
- Well, we're honored
to have you on the show.

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:42.540
So, why have kids books in braille

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:44.340
been so few and far between?

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:46.320
- You know, that was my question.

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:50.460
Like way back in 1980, I met a
mom whose daughter was blind,

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:53.370
and she said they had a hard
time getting books for her

00:00:53.370 --> 00:00:54.900
if they could find them.

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:58.560
They were so expensive, like
100 to $200 each, Kelly.

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:00.180
And that just hurt my heart

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:01.950
because my own kids had, you know,

00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:04.860
you can get books for two, $3.

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:05.693
- Yeah.

00:01:05.693 --> 00:01:08.160
- And that's what kids need,
lots and lots of books.

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:11.070
So, I thought I could do
something about it maybe.

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:14.040
I started a small nonprofit
in my basement in Detroit

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:16.528
called Seedlings Braille
Books for Children,

00:01:16.528 --> 00:01:18.270
making more books available,

00:01:18.270 --> 00:01:20.010
keeping the prices really low,

00:01:20.010 --> 00:01:22.500
and getting more books in kids' hands.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:23.333
- Absolutely.

00:01:23.333 --> 00:01:25.170
That's such a cool
thing that you're doing.

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:27.210
And you have a portion of Seedlings

00:01:27.210 --> 00:01:28.740
that honors your late daughter, right?

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:29.910
Can you tell us about it?

00:01:29.910 --> 00:01:33.324
- Yeah, so my daughters were
one and three years old.

00:01:33.324 --> 00:01:36.404
They're right around your age, Kelly.

00:01:36.404 --> 00:01:41.010
And when I started Seedlings
and then they grew up with it.

00:01:41.010 --> 00:01:44.040
They loved books, they suggested titles.

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:45.840
They worked there in high school.

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:48.240
But when the older one,
Anna went off to college,

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:51.990
unfortunately her car
was hit by a drunk driver

00:01:51.990 --> 00:01:53.880
and she passed.

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:55.887
And of course, I was devastated,

00:01:55.887 --> 00:01:59.100
but with family and faith and Seedlings,

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:02.760
you know, it gave me
things to keep me going.

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:04.830
Lots of people sent memorial donations,

00:02:04.830 --> 00:02:06.750
very generous donations in her name.

00:02:06.750 --> 00:02:10.920
So, we decided to start
a program to honor her.

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:12.960
And we were selling the books at a loss,

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:14.280
maKing the prices low.

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:17.910
But with this new program
called the Book Angel Program,

00:02:17.910 --> 00:02:20.460
we're able to give books away.

00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:22.950
And at first it was
just one book per child

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:24.330
in the United States,

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:26.571
and now it's five books for all the kids

00:02:26.571 --> 00:02:29.520
in the United States and Canada.

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:31.680
So, we're giving away like two thirds

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:33.330
of the books we send out now.

00:02:33.330 --> 00:02:36.690
And it's getting so many
more books in the hands

00:02:36.690 --> 00:02:38.460
of the kids with vision loss.

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:40.020
It's just been wonderful.

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:42.090
- That, it is very
wonderful what you're doing,

00:02:42.090 --> 00:02:43.830
especially in honor of your daughter.

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:44.790
Thank you, Debra.

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:46.590
I'm loving your post right now.

00:02:46.590 --> 00:02:48.360
- Thank you, Kelly, love you.

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:49.530
- Oh, well thank you so much.

00:02:49.530 --> 00:02:50.363
But that's not all.

00:02:50.363 --> 00:02:51.750
Our season long partner Pilot Pen,

00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:53.190
makers of Precise the go-to pen

00:02:53.190 --> 00:02:54.480
of "The Kelly Clarkson Show"

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:57.150
want to honor truly unstoppable
people just like you, ma'am.

00:02:57.150 --> 00:02:59.010
So, they're gonna be writing you a check

00:02:59.010 --> 00:03:01.050
for Seedlings for $1,000.

00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:01.920
How's that sound?

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:05.563
(audience cheering)
- Thank you so much.

00:03:05.563 --> 00:03:08.171
- Yeah, thank you so much, Debra.

00:03:08.171 --> 00:03:09.480
What you're doing is so
cool and so important.

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:12.162
And thank you to all of
our guests this hour.

00:03:12.162 --> 00:03:15.683
Daisy Ridley, Lisa
Vanderpump, Hadley Vlahos,

00:03:15.683 --> 00:03:17.323
Alana and Lawrence Zarian.

00:03:17.323 --> 00:03:18.156
Y'all have a great day.

00:03:18.156 --> 00:03:18.989
If it's not, change it.

00:03:18.989 --> 00:03:20.622
(rock music)

